    kind: invariant  # d1a4
    title: "Codegen wrapper tracing: cross-language linkers must resolve through generated binding/proxy layers"  # d1a4
    status: violated  # d1a4
    priority: 4  # d1a4
    parent:  # d1a4
    tags: []  # d1a4
    before: []  # d1a4
    duplicate_of: []  # d1a4
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d1a4
    pr_ref:  # d1a4
    description: ""  # d1a4
    fields:  # d1a4
      statement: "When a cross-language linker detects a bridge call (IPC, RPC, WASM, codegen), it must trace through generated wrapper/proxy layers to connect the application-level call site to the implementation. Generated bindings that wrap invoke/call/send behind typed functions must not break edge tracing."  # d1a4
      root_cause: "Linkers match literal command names in invoke() calls but codegen tools (specta, contextBridge, graphql-codegen, protoc) generate typed wrapper functions that hide the literal names. Without wrapper resolution, edges terminate at the generated layer instead of reaching the real implementation."  # d1a4
